  "evidencia": "Page: Stefan Edberg. Sentence: Stefan Bengt Edberg (] ; born 19 January 1966) is a Swedish former world no. 1 professional tennis player (in both singles and doubles).\nPage: Stefan Edberg. Sentence: A major proponent of the serve-and-volley style of tennis, he won six Grand Slam singles titles and three Grand Slam men's doubles titles between 1985 and 1996.\nPage: Stefan Edberg. Sentence: He also won the Masters Grand Prix and was a part of the Swedish Davis Cup-winning-team four times.\nPage: Stefan Edberg. Sentence: In addition he won four Masters Series titles, four Championship Series titles and the unofficial Olympic tournament 1984, was ranked in the singles top 10 for ten successive years, 9 years in the top 5, and is considered one of the greatest players of his era.\nPage: Édouard Roger-Vasselin. Sentence: He won the men's doubles title at Roland Garros in 2014, partnering Julien Benneteau.\nPage: 1990 Thriftway ATP Championships – Singles. Sentence: Brad Gilbert was the defending champion but Stefan Edberg defeated him 6–1, 6–1 in the final.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Stefan Edberg. Sentence: Stefan Bengt Edberg (] ; born 19 January 1966) is a Swedish former world no. 1 professional tennis player (in both singles and doubles).\nPage: Stefan Edberg. Sentence: A major proponent of the serve-and-volley style of tennis, he won six Grand Slam singles titles and three Grand Slam men's doubles titles between 1985 and 1996.\nPage: Stefan Edberg. Sentence: He also won the Masters Grand Prix and was a part of the Swedish Davis Cup-winning-team four times.\nPage: Stefan Edberg. Sentence: In addition he won four Masters Series titles, four Championship Series titles and the unofficial Olympic tournament 1984, was ranked in the singles top 10 for ten successive years, 9 years in the top 5, and is considered one of the greatest players of his era.\nPage: Édouard Roger-Vasselin. Sentence: He won the men's doubles title at Roland Garros in 2014, partnering Julien Benneteau.\nPage: 1990 Thriftway ATP Championships – Singles. Sentence: Brad Gilbert was the defending champion but Stefan Edberg defeated him 6–1, 6–1 in the final.",
